+// writer fills the fifo while the reader is not yet attached, the reader then
+// drains that backlog into its own buffer in one go, and because both sides
+// then run at the stream's realtime rate the resulting phase offset never
+// shrinks. Measured input-buffer depth tracks this value closely.
+// 8KB is a bit over two PipeWire quanta at 44100/16/2 (~46ms) - small enough
+// to keep the offset down, large enough to ride out writer scheduling jitter.
+#define PIPE_CAPACITY_BYTES_DEFAULT (8 * 1024)
